Tom: Sure, Mia. Shall we visit the new art museum in the city centre?
Mia: Actually, I went there last month. How about the contemporary art show by the river instead?
Tom: Good idea. I heard a famous self-portrait is being displayed there right now.
Mia: Yes, and the tickets are free for students on Saturdays.
Tom: Perfect. Let''s meet at the bus stop at nine in the morning.
Mia: Great. Don''t forget to bring your camera so we can take some photos.
Tom: I won''t. See you on Saturday!', 'Mia 约 Tom 周六去看艺术;Tom 提议去市中心的新美术馆;Mia 上月去过了,改提议去河边的当代艺术展;那里正展出一幅名人自画像;周六学生门票免费;两人约定早九点在公交站碰面,并带相机拍照。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When are Mia and Tom going to see art?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["On Saturday.","On Sunday.","On Monday.","On Friday."]},{"q":"Where do they finally decide to go?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The new museum in the city centre.","The contemporary art show by the river.","A calligraphy class.","A street art festival."]},{"q":"Why doesn''t Mia want to go to the new museum?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She has already been there recently.","It is closed on Saturdays.","It is much too far away.","The tickets there are expensive."]},{"q":"What is free for students on Saturdays?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The lunch.","The tickets.","The camera.","The bus ride."]},{"q":"Where will the two friends meet?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["At the river gate.","At the school.","At the bus stop.","At Tom''s house."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Ben: Yes, it is. That''s why it is protected behind thick glass.
Anna: Look — so many people are taking photos of it right now.
Ben: I know. They say her eyes seem to follow you around the room.
Anna: That''s a bit strange! Why does she attract so many visitors every day?
Ben: Because of her mysterious smile. One moment she looks happy, the next a little sad.
Anna: Amazing. Who painted her, by the way?
Ben: An Italian artist, hundreds of years ago. The painting is cleaned by experts once a year.
Anna: No wonder the colours still look so fresh.', 'Anna 惊讶蒙娜丽莎比想象的小;Ben 说所以用厚玻璃保护;此刻许多人在拍照;据说她的眼睛仿佛会跟着你;Anna 问为何每天吸引众多游客;Ben 说因为她神秘的微笑,一会儿像高兴一会儿又有点忧伤;画是数百年前一位意大利艺术家所作,每年由专家清洗一次,所以颜色仍鲜亮。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What surprises Anna about the painting?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is smaller than she thought.","It is larger than she thought.","It has no frame.","It is very dark."]},{"q":"Why is the painting kept behind glass?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To make it look bigger.","To keep it safe.","To hide its colours.","To stop people looking."]},{"q":"What does Ben say about her eyes?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are always closed.","They are painted blue.","They seem to follow the viewer.","They look angry."]},{"q":"Why does the painting attract so many visitors?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Its huge size.","Its golden frame.","Its low price.","Her mysterious smile."]},{"q":"How often is the painting cleaned by experts?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Once a year.","Every week.","Every day.","Never at all."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U4', 'fltrp');
Andrew: Honestly, Jill, some of it confused me. The empty room with nothing in it seemed boring.
Jill: Really? I thought that piece was clever. The viewer has to imagine the meaning.
Andrew: Maybe. But the one with everyday objects looked rather lazy to me. The artist didn''t seem to make much.
Jill: I disagree. I think everyday things can also be art if they make us think.
Andrew: Well, my favourite was the living room piece. Looking at the small details really moved me.
Jill: See? So art does mean different things to different people.
Andrew: You''re right about that. That''s exactly what makes it interesting.', 'Jill 问 Andrew 对当代艺术展的看法;Andrew 说有些让他困惑,那间空房什么都没有,觉得无聊;Jill 却觉得那件作品很巧妙,观众要自己想象含义;Andrew 觉得用日常物品的那件很偷懒,艺术家似乎没做什么;Jill 反对,认为日常之物若能引人思考也是艺术;Andrew 最喜欢“客厅”那件,细节让他感动;两人最后认同:艺术对不同的人意味不同,这正是其有趣之处。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did Andrew think of the empty room?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He loved it most.","He thought it was clever.","He found it boring.","He did not see it."]},{"q":"Why did Jill like the empty room?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It was very colourful.","It was extremely large.","It cost a lot of money.","The viewer has to imagine the meaning."]},{"q":"What did Andrew think of the everyday-objects piece?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It seemed lazy.","It was his favourite.","It was too expensive.","It was beautiful."]},{"q":"Which piece was Andrew''s favourite?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The empty room.","The living room piece.","The everyday objects.","The painted wall."]},{"q":"What do Jill and Andrew finally agree on?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Contemporary art is always bad.","Only museums show real art.","Art means different things to different people.","Everyone likes the same art."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U4', 'fltrp');

